<title>UK: NatWest prices 100 mln stg bond for Care Homes No1.</title>
<headline>NatWest prices 100 mln stg bond for Care Homes No1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following collateralised bond, announced earlier by lead manager NatWest Markets, has been priced.</p>
<p>LEAD MGR  NATWEST MARKETS</p>
<p>BORROWER  CARE HOMES NO. 1</p>
<p>TRANCHE A1</p>
<p> AMT    60 MLN STG    COUPON     8.0	 MATURITY	.APR.21</p>
<p> D&amp;P RATING AAA	 ISS PRICE  99.42     PAY DATE    09.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.625     REOFFER    99.42     SPREAD	+60 BP</p>
<p>TRANCHE A2</p>
<p> AMT    40 MLN STG    COUPON     8.50	MATURITY	.APR.21</p>
<p> D&amp;P RATING BBB	 ISS PRICE  98.941    PAY DATE    09.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.625     REOFFER    98.941    SPREAD	+115 BP</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/UK/CI</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  UK	  TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 8.0 PCT GILT DUE 2021</p>
<p> NOTES	THE NOTES ARE COLLATERALISED BY LEASES ON NURSING</p>
<p>		HOME PROPERTIES.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
